new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..1995d86465
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/src/router/reaper_fwsim/witness.static
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# reaper_fwsim static witnesses - the promises every router makes, as packets.
+# One row per line: id|feature|fam|in|src|dst|proto|port|ct|expect|out|mac|requires
+# shape rows:       id|feature|fam|shape|<predicate>|||||OK
+# Placeholders are resolved from the router's own addresses at run time; a row
+# whose placeholder has no value (no IPv6, no WAN address yet) is reported as
+# n/a, never as red. `in` = ingress interface, or `gen` for the router's own
+# traffic. $LANMAC is a device an armed Gatekeeper allows (empty when it is
+# off); $V6 exists only while the LAN has a global IPv6 prefix. Rows that
+# depend on a setting (WAN ping, WAN management, port forwards, Gatekeeper,
+# Warden, guests, VPN servers) are generated in reaper_fwsim.c from the live
+# configuration, not listed here.
+#
+# The two fields to get right are the ingress interface and the conntrack
+# state: a witness that is vague about either passes on paper and fails on a
+# client. Catalog: docs/backlog/firewall-witness-catalog.md (archive).
+# expect: ACCEPT (no translation), DROP, RESOLVED (answered at the router or
+# handed to an intercept target and forwarded), DNAT, DNAT+ACCEPT.
+
+# ---- A. core reachability -------------------------------------------------
+A1|LAN host reaches the WAN|4|$LANIF|$LANHOST|1.1.1.1|tcp|443|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC
+A2|Reply from the WAN reaches the LAN host|4|$WANIF|1.1.1.1|$LANHOST|tcp|40000|ESTABLISHED|ACCEPT
+A3|LAN host resolves DNS at the router|4|$LANIF|$LANHOST|$RTR|udp|53|NEW|RESOLVED||$LANMAC
+A4|Unsolicited WAN traffic never reaches a LAN host|4|$WANIF|$WANSRC|$LANHOST|tcp|445|NEW|DROP
+A5|LAN host reaches the router's web interface|4|$LANIF|$LANHOST|$RTR|tcp|80|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC
+A9|The router's own outbound traffic leaves|4|gen|$RTR|1.1.1.1|tcp|443|NEW|ACCEPT
+A11|LAN host gets DHCP from the router|4|$LANIF|0.0.0.0|255.255.255.255|udp|67|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC
+H2|Advisor port 5152 is closed to the LAN|4|$LANIF|$LANHOST|$RTR|tcp|5152|NEW|DROP||$LANMAC
+
+# ---- IPv6 (n/a while the router has no IPv6) ------------------------------
+A1v6|LAN host reaches the WAN over IPv6|6|$LANIF|$LAN6HOST|2606:4700:4700::1111|tcp|443|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC
+A3v6|LAN host resolves DNS at the router over IPv6|6|$LANIF|$LAN6HOST|$RTR6|udp|53|NEW|RESOLVED||$LANMAC
+A4v6|Unsolicited WAN IPv6 traffic never reaches a LAN host|6|$WANIF|$WAN6SRC|$LAN6HOST|tcp|445|NEW|DROP
+A6v6|WAN IPv6 management is closed|6|$WANIF|$WAN6SRC|$WAN6IP|tcp|80|NEW|DROP
+A10a|Router advertisements from the WAN are accepted|6|$WANIF|fe80::1|ff02::1|icmpv6|134|NEW|ACCEPT|||$V6
+A10b|Router solicitations from the LAN are accepted|6|$LANIF|fe80::2|ff02::2|icmpv6|133|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC|$V6
+A10c|Neighbour solicitations from the LAN are accepted|6|$LANIF|fe80::2|ff02::1:ff00:1|icmpv6|135|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC|$V6
+A10d|Neighbour advertisements from the LAN are accepted|6|$LANIF|$LAN6HOST|$RTR6|icmpv6|136|NEW|ACCEPT||$LANMAC|$V6
