+RFW_292=Example: a Gatekeeper-blocked device must not reach the WAN (drop) but must still resolve names at the router (accept). If that second row turns red, the DNS carve-out sits behind the block - the rule column names what caught it.
+RFW_293=The filter table is the boot-time skeleton: the full ruleset never loaded. Port forwards, VPN server chains and the DoS guard are not in force.
+RFW_294=Re-check now
+RFW_295=Rows marked depends sit behind a match the walker does not model (string, u32, time, policy) and are not judged. n/a means the router has no such network yet. Nothing on this tab changes the firewall.
